5,\"_76\":77,\"_78\":159},{\"_74\":75,\"_76\":77,\"_78\":150},{\"_74\":75,\"_76\":77,\"_78\":144},{\"_74\":75,\"_76\":77,\"_78\":135},{\"_74\":75,\"_76\":77,\"_78\":126},{\"_74\":75,\"_76\":77,\"_78\":117},{\"_74\":75,\"_76\":77,\"_78\":108},{\"_74\":75,\"_76\":77,\"_78\":95},{\"_74\":75,\"_76\":77,\"_78\":79},\"kind\",\"callout\",\"variant\",\"transparent\",\"children\",[80,81],{\"_74\":88,\"_89\":90,\"_91\":-7,\"_78\":92},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":83},\"p\",[84],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":86,\"_87\":-7},\"text\",\"Models can be updated or retired over time. If a model is no longer available, GPTs are automatically switched to a similar current model.\",\"marks\",\"h\",\"level\",2,\"anchorId\",[93],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":94,\"_87\":-7},\"Why don’t I see the same model options as before?\",[96,97,98],{\"_74\":88,\"_89\":90,\"_91\":-7,\"_78\":105},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":102},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":99},[100],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":101,\"_87\":-7},\"New GPT creation is unavailable on personal ChatGPT accounts, regardless of subscription.\",[103],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":104,\"_87\":-7},\"You can continue using GPTs you previously created. Editing an existing GPT still depends on your subscription and permissions, so changing to a plan that does not support editing may prevent you from making changes.\",[106],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":107,\"_87\":-7},\"What happens to my existing GPTs if I change or cancel my subscription?\",[109,110],{\"_74\":88,\"_89\":90,\"_91\":-7,\"_78\":114},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":111},[112],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":113,\"_87\":-7},\"GPTs do not use saved memory, custom instructions, or previous conversations. Each conversation starts fresh.\",[115],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":116,\"_87\":-7},\"Do GPTs use memory or custom instructions?\",[118,119],{\"_74\":88,\"_89\":90,\"_91\":-7,\"_78\":123},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":120},[121],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":122,\"_87\":-7},\"Yes. On ChatGPT web, you can type @ in a conversation to bring in a GPT without starting a new chat. Your next message will go to that GPT, and the conversation keeps its current context. This @-mention flow isn’t available in the iOS or Android apps. On mobile, open the GPT from the GPTs menu or sidebar instead.\",[124],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":125,\"_87\":-7},\"Can I use a GPT from a regular ChatGPT conversation?\",[127,128],{\"_74\":88,\"_89\":90,\"_91\":-7,\"_78\":132},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":129},[130],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":131,\"_87\":-7},\"GPTs are no-code assistants built and used inside ChatGPT. Assistants built with the API are developer-built integrations that use OpenAI models inside a website or service outside of ChatGPT.\",[133],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":134,\"_87\":-7},\"What’s the difference between GPTs and assistants built with the API?\",[136,137],{\"_74\":88,\"_89\":90,\"_91\":-7,\"_78\":141},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":138},[139],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":140,\"_87\":-7},\"GPTs are designed to work in ChatGPT. They are not a way to embed ChatGPT in an external website or application. To build an assistant into a product, use the API.\",[142],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":143,\"_87\":-7},\"Can I embed my GPT on my website?\",[145],{\"_74\":88,\"_89\":146,\"_91\":-7,\"_78\":147},1,[148],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":149,\"_87\":-7},\"FAQ\",[151,152],{\"_74\":88,\"_89\":90,\"_91\":-7,\"_78\":156},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":153},[154],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":155,\"_87\":-7},\"GPTs can be integrated with apps and external APIs. When you interact with a GPT that uses apps or external APIs, relevant parts of your input may be sent to the third-party service. Depending on the GPT's setup and the type of action, ChatGPT may ask you to approve the request before information is sent or the action runs. OpenAI does not audit or control how those services use or store your data. Only use GPTs with APIs or apps that you trust.\",[157],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":158,\"_87\":-7},\"External APIs and apps\",[160,161],{\"_74\":88,\"_89\":90,\"_91\":-7,\"_78\":171},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":162},[163,164,165],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":170,\"_87\":-7},{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":167,\"_87\":168},{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":166,\"_87\":-7},\" individual conversations that users have with their GPTs.\",\"cannot view\",[169],\"b\",\"GPT builders \",[172],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":173,\"_87\":-7},\"Conversation access\",[175,176],{\"_74\":88,\"_89\":90,\"_91\":-7,\"_78\":188},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":177},[178,179,180],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":187,\"_87\":-7},{\"_74\":182,\"_27\":183,\"_78\":184},{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":181,\"_87\":-7},\".\",\"a\",\"https://help.openai.com/articles/7730893\",[185],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":186,\"_87\":-7},\"Data Controls FAQ\",\"Whether conversations with a GPT may be used to improve OpenAI’s models depends on the plan you are using.\\n\\nFor Business, Enterprise, and Edu plans, data is not used for training by default.\\n\\nFor consumer plans, including Free, Plus, Go, and Pro, data may be used for training depending on whether you have opted out. To opt out or learn more, see: \",[189],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":190,\"_87\":-7},\"Model training\",[192],{\"_74\":88,\"_89\":146,\"_91\":-7,\"_78\":193},[194],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":195,\"_87\":-7},\"Privacy and data use\",[197,198],{\"_74\":88,\"_89\":90,\"_91\":-7,\"_78\":208},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":199},[200,201,202],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":207,\"_87\":-7},{\"_74\":182,\"_27\":203,\"_78\":204},{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":181,\"_87\":-7},\"https://help.openai.com/articles/11325361\",[205],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":206,\"_87\":-7},\"Troubleshooting GPTs\",\"For information on common issues, how to troubleshoot them, and how to report content or other issues, see: \",[209],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":210,\"_87\":-7},\"Troubleshooting and reporting issues\",[212,213],{\"_74\":88,\"_89\":90,\"_91\":-7,\"_78\":223},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":214},[215,216,217],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":222,\"_87\":-7},{\"_74\":182,\"_27\":218,\"_78\":219},{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":181,\"_87\":-7},\"https://help.openai.com/articles/8555535\",[220],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":221,\"_87\":-7},\"Managing GPT access in Enterprise and Edu workspaces\",\"GPT access and sharing may be limited by workspace settings and permissions. Admins or owners may control which GPTs users can access, what options appear in the GPT editor, and which sharing methods are available. For detailed information, see: \",[224],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":225,\"_87\":-7},\"Workspace controls (Enterprise and Edu)\",[227,228,229,230],{\"_74\":88,\"_89\":90,\"_91\":-7,\"_78\":246},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":243},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":240},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":231},[232,233,234],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":239,\"_87\":-7},{\"_74\":182,\"_27\":235,\"_78\":236},{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":181,\"_87\":-7},\"https://help.openai.com/articles/8798878\",[237],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":238,\"_87\":-7},\"Sharing and publishing GPTs\",\"For step-by-step guidance on sharing options, public publishing requirements, Builder Profiles, and GPT Store publishing, see: \",[241],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":242,\"_87\":-7},\"In Business, Enterprise, and Edu workspaces, GPT sharing and publishing options continue to depend on workspace settings and permissions. Available options may include sharing with specific people, sharing within a workspace, sharing by link, or publishing to the GPT Store when permitted.\",[244],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":245,\"_87\":-7},\"GPT sharing options depend on your account, plan, and workspace settings. Personal ChatGPT accounts, including Free, Go, Plus, and Pro, cannot publish new GPTs.\",[247],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":248,\"_87\":-7},\"Sharing and publishing\",[250,251,252,253,254],{\"_74\":88,\"_89\":90,\"_91\":-7,\"_78\":298},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":295},{\"_74\":268,\"_269\":270},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":264},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":255},[256,257,258],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":263,\"_87\":-7},{\"_74\":182,\"_27\":259,\"_78\":260},{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":181,\"_87\":-7},\"https://help.openai.com/articles/8554397\",[261],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":262,\"_87\":-7},\"Creating and editing GPTs\",\"For step-by-step instructions on building, editing, testing, and updating a GPT, see: \",[265],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":266,\"_87\":267},\"New GPT creation is not available on personal ChatGPT accounts, including Free, Go, Plus, and Pro.\",[169],\"ul\",\"items\",[271,272,273,274],[291],[283],[279],[275],{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":276},[277],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":278,\"_87\":-7},\"After configuring a GPT, test it in preview and save changes.\",{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":280},[281],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":282,\"_87\":-7},\"GPTs can be built conversationally or configured directly in the editor.\",{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":284},[285,286,287],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":290,\"_87\":-7},{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":288,\"_87\":289},{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":181,\"_87\":-7},\"Create\",[169],\"Select \",{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":292},[293],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":294,\"_87\":-7},\"Open the GPTs area in ChatGPT\",[296],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":297,\"_87\":-7},\"To create a GPT:\",[299],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":300,\"_87\":-7},\"Creating a GPT in a managed workspace\",[302,303,304,305],{\"_74\":88,\"_89\":90,\"_91\":-7,\"_78\":333},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":330},{\"_74\":268,\"_269\":309},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":306},[307],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":308,\"_87\":-7},\"After opening a GPT, users can review its description or conversation starters to understand what it is designed to do, then send a message to begin chatting. The GPT will respond based on its configured instructions, knowledge, and enabled capabilities.\",[310,311,312],[321],[317],[313],{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":314},[315],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":316,\"_87\":-7},\"Open a GPT that has been shared with them in their workspace.\",{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":318},[319],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":320,\"_87\":-7},\"Use a direct link to a GPT.\",{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":322},[323,324,325],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":329,\"_87\":-7},{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":327,\"_87\":328},{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":326,\"_87\":-7},\" in ChatGPT to browse available GPTs.\",\"Explore GPTs\",[169],\"Open \",[331],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":332,\"_87\":-7},\"Users can access a GPT in several ways.\",[334],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":335,\"_87\":-7},\"Using a GPT\",[337],{\"_74\":88,\"_89\":146,\"_91\":-7,\"_78\":338},[339],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":340,\"_87\":-7},\"Getting started\",[342,343,344,345],{\"_74\":88,\"_89\":146,\"_91\":-7,\"_78\":401},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":398},{\"_74\":268,\"_269\":349},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":346},[347],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":348,\"_87\":-7},\"A GPT can use either apps or actions, but not both at the same time.\",[350,351,352,353,354,355],[391],[384],[377],[370],[363],[356],{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":357},[358,359],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":361,\"_87\":362},{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":360,\"_87\":-7},\" Ways a GPT can connect to external APIs you define.\",\"Actions:\",[169],{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":364},[365,366],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":368,\"_87\":369},{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":367,\"_87\":-7},\" Ways a GPT can connect to outside services through user-connected tools.\",\"Apps:\",[169],{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":371},[372,373],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":375,\"_87\":376},{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":374,\"_87\":-7},\" Selected tools or features, such as web search or image generation.\",\"Capabilities:\",[169],{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":378},[379,380],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":382,\"_87\":383},{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":381,\"_87\":-7},\" Uploaded files the GPT can use as reference when answering questions.\",\"Knowledge:\",[169],{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":385},[386,387],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":389,\"_87\":390},{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":388,\"_87\":-7},\" Provide example prompts to help users get started.\",\"Conversation starters:\",[169],{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":392},[393,394],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":396,\"_87\":397},{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":395,\"_87\":-7},\" Define the GPT’s behavior, tone, goals, and boundaries.\",\"Instructions:\",[169],[399],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":400,\"_87\":-7},\"A GPT can include several configuration elements that shape how it behaves and what it can do.\",[402],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":403,\"_87\":-7},\"What a GPT can include\",[405,406,407,408],{\"_74\":88,\"_89\":90,\"_91\":-7,\"_78\":424},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":415},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":412},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":409},[410],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":411,\"_87\":-7},\"In Business, Enterprise, and Edu workspaces, GPT creation, editing, and publishing depend on workspace settings and permissions.\",[413],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":414,\"_87\":-7},\"Existing GPTs remain available to use. Editing an existing GPT continues to require an eligible subscription and any applicable account or workspace permissions.\",[416,417,418],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":423,\"_87\":-7},{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":421,\"_87\":422},{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":419,\"_87\":420},\"New GPT creation and publishing are not available on personal ChatGPT accounts, including Free, Go, Plus, and Pro.\",[169],\"\\n\",[169],\"GPTs are available to all ChatGPT users, but users must be signed in to start a conversation. Public GPT pages may be visible without signing in, but users are prompted to sign in before chatting.\\n\\nOnce signed in, users can interact with any GPT they have access to, including GPTs that are public, shared with them directly, or available through workspace settings.\\n\",[425],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":426,\"_87\":-7},\"Availability\",[428,429],{\"_74\":88,\"_89\":146,\"_91\":-7,\"_78\":433},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":430},[431],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":432,\"_87\":-7},\"GPTs (also called custom GPTs) are versions of ChatGPT configured for a specific purpose. A GPT can combine specific instructions, knowledge, and selected capabilities to create a more tailored experience in ChatGPT.\",[434],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":435,\"_87\":-7},\"Overview\",\"blue\",[438,439],{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":450},{\"_74\":82,\"_78\":440},[441,442,443],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":449,\"_87\":-7},{\"_74\":182,\"_27\":445,\"_78\":446},{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":444,\"_87\":-7},\". \",\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001519\",[447],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":448,\"_87\":-7},\"Read more\",\"Other plans are expected to follow the same timeline - review notices, when available, for your account or workspace. Public GPTs created in affected Enterprise workspaces are included even when used from another plan. \",[451,452,453],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":461,\"_87\":-7},{\"_74\":182,\"_27\":455,\"_78\":456},{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":454,\"_87\":-7},\". The migration experience is targeted for Sep 17, 2026 and may not be available to every account or workspace at the same time. Migrate, test, and review access to the replacement before switching.\",\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001256\",[457],{\"_74\":85,\"_85\":458,\"_87\":459},\"plugins\",[460],\"u\",\"We’re planning to retire custom GPTs and help you build on the workflows you’ve already created. Instead of custom GPTs, we recommend moving your workflows to Plugins. Plugins offer a way to bring reusable instructions and connected apps together, so your guidance can work alongside the tools and information a task needs. A migration flow is planned to help you make that move.\\n\\nFor affected Enterprise workspaces, retirement is planned for Dec 11, 2026. Existing GPTs remain usable until retirement. Start preparing the workflows you want to keep for migration to \",\"supportedLanguages\",[20,464,465,466,467,468,469,470,471,472,473,474,475,476,477,478,479,480,481,482,483,484,485,486,487,488,489,490,491,492,493,494,495,496,497,498,499,500,501,502,503,504,505,506,507,508,509,510,511,512,513,514,515,516,517,518,519,520,521,522,523,524,525,526,527,528,529],\"ar\",\"ja-jp\",\"es-es\",\"es-419\",\"de-de\",\"bn-bd\",\"fr-ca\",\"fr-fr\",\"hi-in\",\"id-id\",\"it-it\",\"kn-in\",\"ko-kr\",\"mr-in\",\"pt-br\",\"pt-pt\",\"ru-ru\",\"ta-in\",\"te-in\",\"zh-hans-cn\",\"zh-hant\",\"zh-hant-hk\",\"sq-al\",\"am-et\",\"hy-am\",\"bs-ba\",\"bg-bg\",\"my-mm\",\"ca-es\",\"hr-hr\",\"cs-cz\",\"da-dk\",\"nl-nl\",\"et-ee\",\"fil-ph\",\"fa-ir\",\"fi-fi\",\"ka-ge\",\"el-gr\",\"gu-in\",\"hu-hu\",\"is-is\",\"ga-ie\",\"jv-id\",\"kk-cyrl\",\"lv-lv\",\"lt-lt\",\"mk-mk\",\"ms-my\",\"ml-in\",\"mt-mt\",\"mn-mn\",\"nb-no\",\"pl-pl\",\"pa-in\",\"ro-ro\",\"sk-sk\",\"sl-si\",\"so-dj\",\"sw-ke\",\"sv-se\",\"th-th\",\"tr-tr\",\"uk-ua\",\"ur-in\",\"vi-vn\",\"sessionId\",\"bb6b958d-24b2-4ea6-97ee-603344fecef6\",\"sessionIdToken\",\"v1.bb6b958d-24b2-4ea6-97ee-603344fecef6.WmiOjF-yVPrt